course: dictionary
lesson: 4262
title: Gratitude: the feeling of thanks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gratitude is a noun. It means the feeling of being thankful for something good that someone did or gave you. You can feel gratitude inside, and you can show it by saying thank you.
explain: «Gratitude means noticing good things and saying thank you; grateful people tend to be happier and kinder.» The clue words are noticing good things and saying thank you. Those are the actions that show gratitude. Grateful is the describing word, the adjective, for a person who feels gratitude.
explain: Look at the phrases around the word. «Presents are received with gratitude» means the presents are taken with a thankful heart. Other phrases to spot are show gratitude, out of gratitude, and a gratitude journal. To check your meaning, swap thankfulness into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Gratitude means the feeling of being thankful for something good.
fact: Gratitude is uncountable, so we say «a lot of gratitude», not «two gratitudes».
fact: Common phrases are «show gratitude», «with gratitude», «out of gratitude», and «a gratitude journal».
fact: «Grateful» is the adjective: «She was grateful for the help.»
fact: Noticing good things and saying thank you can help people feel happier and kinder.
exercise: «Presents are received with gratitude.» What does with gratitude mean here? | Secretly, in a hidden box | Quickly, before anyone else can grab them | Angrily, because the presents were too small | *Thankfully, with a thankful heart
exercise: Which action is a good way to show gratitude? | *Saying thank you and smiling | Asking for something bigger | Ignoring the gift | Hiding the present under the bed
exercise: Which word is the adjective that describes a person who feels gratitude? | Grating | *Grateful | Gratitude | Grater
test: What does gratitude mean? | Being very angry about something unfair | Feeling tired after a long day | Asking for more presents than anyone else | *The feeling of being thankful for something good
test: Which sentence uses gratitude correctly? | *She wrote in her gratitude journal every night. | Gratitudes is a fun word to say. | He gratitude the bus driver. | She had five gratitudes in the box.
exam: Mia's gran gave her a birthday present, and Mia replied with gratitude. Why is this a good reply? | Because Mia gave the present back | *Because Mia showed thankfulness for something good | Because Mia wanted a bigger present | Because Mia said nothing at all
